A||||46||CUTTER||FieroGT   Vs.   Integra V-Tech||||1||
Z||000000||CUTTER||04-24-2000||02:42 AM||||My friend has a 96-97 acura integra v-tech 40,000 miles 5spd and he said he wanted to cruise down to the getty mart down town. I always wanted to race him so I figured I will drive my 87GT stock auto and try to get him to race. he followed behind me and we hit a red light, I reved it up and turned around to see his face...he reved and shook his head yes, I was like "oh my...here we go a loss for me" the light turned green and I nailed it and hit about 30 and looked back, he was about 2 car lengths behind me, I hit 70-80 and looked in rearview and he was about the same then he left off and so did I. When we got back to my house he said he was on it full throttle and redlined it every gear to 85-90mph (these things redline at like 8-9000 rpm's. He says he has 170 HP, and my car is stock, so what do you guys think? I thought I would get whooped, am I underestimating my 87GT?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||04-24-2000||02:53 AM||||Dont the V6 Fieros run high 15s in the 1/4 mile?<P>The Integra V-Tech runs low 16s...<P>That would put you ahead by about 2 cars.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> <P>By the way good job...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||CUTTER||04-24-2000||02:57 AM||||You should see the smile on my face now...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||04-24-2000||03:16 AM||||A v6 Fiero in good shape should be able to run mid-15's, right?<P>the problem with those imports is that they have <B>no</B> low end torque.. on the freeway he might have taken you, but street racing?  yeah right..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  that's why I just have to shake my head at anyone who marvels at that honda s2000.. sure, it's nice, but you have to launch it at 5-6,000 rpm to get anywhere.. not quite the most street friendly.. I'd hate to get caught in a traffic jam with that thing..<P>ok, I'm done ranting now<BR>&lt;stepping down from my bar of soap&gt;  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan86gt3.8||04-24-2000||05:50 PM||||you are correct.  they can redline it till 23,000 will they ever have low end torque? NO!!!!!!!!!!  Thats why a good ole american v6 (give me pushrods or give me death) ohv engines win stoplight races.  What the ricers don't know is that our friend Mr toque is one that you want ridin shotgun with you at a light.  Thats prolly why I beat an awd turbo eclipse (2nd generation GSX).  I know yall have heard about it before and might be tired of it, but he didn't get in front of me till 85-90 mph, which would have ben the 1/4 mile mark. So wind it up all you want but untill you have some low end torque don't bother racing at lights. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||04-25-2000||02:19 AM||||yep.  Just had a friendly little race with a guy I work with tonight.  Eclipse GS Spyder, 97 or 98.  I was behind him in the left turn lane.. Light turned green, he swung into the outside lane, I flew by him on the inside.  yeee-ha!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  can't wait to tease him about my 14 year old car with 145,000 miles on it beating his nice new one..muhahaha||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sleeper||04-25-2000||04:17 AM||||Race some ricers out here and they'll be the ones laughing, not to give them alotta props but my nights at the street races have given me some respect to ricers, and I hate them with a passion...bottles are for babies!||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||04-25-2000||10:24 AM||||BOTTLES ARE FOR BABIES!!!  i loved my bottle! turned my daily driver in to a Fire breathing stop-light monster! pushed me from 14.7 to 13.6!! 1/10 faster and i'd need a helmet according to NHRA rules... Bottles are for ANYONE with the guts to squeeze it. NITROUS ROCKS!  Meet some lame kid at the light and pick up your front tires and they ALL run away! Can't wait for the 4:10 install!!!  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Sleeper||04-25-2000||01:25 PM||||NOS is the CHEATER system, it's for people who can't build their motor (like ricers). Even in Pro Street right now all the people with NOS are getting smoked by people with turbos and super chargers...also it burns up your rings and messes up your connecting rods and pistons, so if you like to rebuild alot, this is your ticket. Not trying to be mean, I just dislike NOS and sometimes the user.||||reg||1
Z||000009||superXmotorsports||04-25-2000||03:57 PM||||turbos can sure damage a motor too!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  If NOS is used properly I think it is a good thing.  Just don't add a 150HP shot to a motor with 100k miles (you get the point).  I plan to add a 50HP shot (computer programmed only to operate at WOT) to my 99 Spyder this summer.  SXM.||||reg||1
Z||000010||87PegasusGT||04-25-2000||04:01 PM||||Sleeper:<BR>Not to start a war or anything, but having done my research both on designing turbo systems and NOS systems, I will have to debate you on that issue. NOS does no more damage than a normal turbo kit will do DEPENDING on how you use it. By increasing the oxygen/amount of fuel detonated/compression, you will bring some wear and tear.In order to have an efficient NOS setup, you must do the research to know what your engine can take and build the heads, use the correct cam etc to match your NOS intake. It is just as much of a science as turbos. On the same token, anyone can buy a turbo setup, but if you run too much psi for your stock engine, you will break stuff also. They both do the same thing although one compresses atmosheric air for more oxygen and NOS just injects it in a concentrated dose. If money was no issue, I would take the turbo, but NOS is a scientific tool to be utilized like anything else. If you tell a turbo guy that using ice to cool his intercooler for free hp that he is a CHEATER, then you should also use this term on cold air intake systems and every other technological advancement that must be studied before it is used.  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||88formula||04-25-2000||05:18 PM||||I agree with 87PegasusGT, I have done a fare share of research on supercharging, turbo charging, and nitrous. They are all forms of forced induction so when someone says nitrous is cheating than so is the guy with a turbo and the guy with a supercharger. Nitrous shortening the life of your engine, guess what? All these things shorten the life of your engine; the more power your engine makes the shorter your engines life will be.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||stimpy||04-25-2000||08:00 PM||||Jeez, I feel an aura of Deja Vu comng along. The old "cheating" debate. My vote is all is fair in love, war, and horsepower. Throwing comments aound like that is no different then the morons who say that Fieros are POS that always catch on fire etc etc. Sleeper, take it easy. There aren't a whole lot of options when building up a 2.8. Sure, my heads are ported and I've got all the nifty forged pistons and rods in a good rebuild, but it ain't enough to really snap the neck back. I could go turbo or nitrous, but neither way is "all motor". Do I care? Uh, no. I just wanna light the fires and smoke the tires baby boy! <P>And if for some reason, that makes you not like me, I'll be in my room crying into my pillow...NOT!!!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Dan86gt3.8||04-25-2000||09:08 PM||||ohhh no not the good ole nos debate once again.  I might have to call shaun out he loves this one.  Anywhoo see the thing is this:  it all comes down to opinion. Last time this debate came around someone mentioned the street racing rule book which tells you what can and can't be run.  I like the old "run what ya brung" slogan.  I mean if a punk in a civic beats me with a 200 sot I'm not gona fell too bad.  I have thought about using nos before, and I still might.  Its cheap hp is all it boils down too. and contrary to popular beief reasonable shots are not gona blow the motor the first time you hit the switch.  And as far is under rating ricers yes I am gona do it because where I live they are all chumps, now I am sure if I cruised the bigger cities some might be run 25 psi in there talon and clicking off 11's or whatever, but untill I move to so. Cali or to houston or dallas or something, I will laugh at ricers.  Anyway have fun with the debate hopefully it will go en fuego!||||reg||1
