Z||000022||Sleeper||04-25-2000||11:36 PM||||no one really wants to race me, to be honest, I rev on ricers and sometimes hot rods at stop lights, usually they shake their head no, my dad and friends say my fiero looks to threating or something, I have a 85 GT, my motor is stock except for a accel super coil, I put in a J.E.T. superchip awhile back, I got my exhaust redone last year with some resonator tips so its pretty loud, I read a article once and found out how to lighten a fiero, so I ripped out a bunch of Sh*t for that reason and for better cooling the engine thats about it, I'm gonna lower it next week and oh did I mention it's competition yellow with black racing strips and a FIERO MOTORSTPORTS stick on the front windshield.<P>I was kinda waiting for that Sleeper name thingy, it's just a name that first came to my head on my first post, my friend has a sleep though, 65 chevelle, pretty dope, and another one of my friends had a 65 falcon that was pretty dope too.<P>And oh, as much as I hate to admit NOS is the ulimate sleeper.<p>[This message has been edited by Sleeper (edited 04-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||stimpy||04-25-2000||11:47 PM||||Sounds like yer ride is pretty slick. You may catch some ricer hell for the Pontiac motorsports decal, but not from me, I got one too. I also agee about not getting many takers on stoplight shennanigins. I have a flowmaster and 3" pipe through the exhaust system so most rice races go like this... Red light: rice boy exhaust revving to 7000 "wee wee weez'; my exhaust "boom badda wadaa VROOM" up to 2500. Green light the turn into little speck as they creep across the intersection.<P>I still want a nitro burning Geo Metro though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ||||reg||1
