Z||000030||Richard Parnell||04-26-2000||03:38 AM||||Try racing a V8 Fiero.  As some know I haven't gotten my 350 installed yet, but a Fiero mechanic here in Honolulu I know has a V8 in his fiero.  He races motorcycles at the drags and beats them.  Fastest ride I've ever been in.  Doesn't accelerate from here to there.  It's just POW and you're from there to here with your head spinning and it sounds great! I can't wait, I'm just bidding my time to surprise some smarts alecs in their Monte Carlo and Camaro big hunks of metal.||||reg||6
Z||000031||Haze_Performance||04-26-2000||05:02 AM||||Im not a big nitrous fan but there is nothing worng with it. Its NOT for cheaters. If that is the case then Turbos and Chargers are cheating too right? (I DONT THINK SO) Some guys think that the only real race car is one with no power adders. Give me a break people build a car with the amount of money they can afford. If a guy wants to put spray in his Geo and race it let him. I had a 24lb ProCharger in my 88 Mustang and no one could beat me on the street. But I still never looked down on the little guy. If all you can afford is a ricer with NOS have fun with it..We all started somwhere..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  (now its time for people to yell at me)||||reg||14
Z||000032||superXmotorsports||04-26-2000||01:23 PM||||Maybe someday we could define 'ricer' so I can make sure if one of you see me sometime in my Eclipse you won't try to run me off the road!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  There are TACKY modified cars of all makes / models.  I think there are some awesome Japanesse produced vehicles:<BR>late model Toyota Supra twin turbo<BR>Acura NSX<BR>Skyline GT-R<BR>Mazda RX7<BR>Nissan 300ZX twin turbo<BR>(and of course 1999 Mitsubushi Eclipse Spyder)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>You see PLENTY of made in the USA Cavaliers and Neons that look like crap too!<P>SXM.||||reg||1
Z||000033||1FST2M6||04-26-2000||02:02 PM||||GOOD GRIEF GUYS! to define ricer see..  <A HREF="http://www.riceboypage.com" TARGET=_blank>www.riceboypage.com</A>   those of you that think you can hear a supercharger are just trying to convince yourself that your right. My Magnusen, along with MANY other manufactures spend LOTS of money keeping thier units quiet. I see/deal with S/C Hondas and Acuras on a daily basis and not a single one of them has a tell tale whine of a supercharger. And 3 of them are running between 9 and 14psi on a STOCK MOTOR!  Weiand makers of the small and big block roots type, machine the gears in their units to make their signature whine. And a mustang/Camaro with a centrifugal type MAY whine if they have more than 9psi. Or are using a COGED belt. Turbo motors are quiet by nature, unless they are equipped with an external blow-off valve. (not stock waste gate) My sail panels say NOS. so anyone paying attention will lay off. and those that THINK they have a chance... well show em your tail lights and they stick their tail between their legs and hide.  Meet a 14 year old car at the light with a big sticker in the back window and deep exhaust note tells everone "leave me alone" if they want to pick a fight they better have big arms!and gnads bigger than the guy next to him. and please.. be willing to say you lost... this "i missed a shift" or "well my car didn't hook up" crap if just the reason you were "behind" me LOSING! Thats all part of racing.. the abilty to control your car better than you neighbor in the next lane. and a better car doen't hurt. I don't think nitrous is cheating. My car lets everone know. It's not hard on your motor IF its correctly set up. I've gone 6000+ miles through 16+ bottles of nitrous and check the compression at LEAST once a month and i have NOT lost ANY pressure since it's install. in june of last year. I now have 97,500 miles on the car. Turbos are more distructive than Nitrous. thier varying compression and bearing load OVER AND OVER will wear out bearings faster then short bursts of nitrous. I was told that buy the motor builder at the shop. He builds Turbo motors for a living... James. <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  for nothings cheating unless your bitter cause you lost. If you pick a fight at a light you have to be willing to lose. no matter what your upaginst, be it a Twingo, a TVR,a ratty old big block chevette whatever.    ||||reg||1
Z||000034||1FST2M6||04-26-2000||02:11 PM||||yeah what Haze just said... just cause hes in an import or "econo box" doens't mean your better... your only better if you don't do that LAME fly-by after you lose! Stop and talk to whom ever your competing with to find out what your up aginst. or to congradulate or pick on...  "Dam you smoked me.. what cha got in there?" - or - "you got SPANKED by a 14 year old car!"  <P> Always appreciate, never expect||||reg||1
