Z||000042||Spyder||04-28-2000||12:19 PM||||Sorry, I'm off topic, oh well.<BR>Frontal:<BR>Yes it’s my wife’s car, she lets me drive it,    sometimes.<BR>But Look close at the pic, uh oh, orange calipers.<BR>You can’t see the exhaust, looks stock, but has a loud rumble.<BR>Nope, NO NO NO NO STICKERS.<P>As far as the VehiCross, I’m not touching it, but a turbo would be nice.<BR>(got to hit that lotto first)<P>Standard, The Z is Naturally Aspirated. I wish it was twin turbo.<P>And here’s why it is a NA.<BR>About five years ago, My wife (girlfriend then) was following me home one day after work (in her car) I looked in my rear view mirror, she was gone.  I turn my head around to see her already out of her Tracker peeking into the window of that Z.  I had been seeing it there for over a week and I thought that it was less than a year old and out of my price range $$$$$. That’s why I never stopped.  I turned around and talked to the owner who bought it new for his wife.  The only reason they were selling it was his wife who just turned 50 wanted the convertible Z.  It was a steal, we bought it the next day. <BR>You guys want to here the scary part, it’s a 1990, that car was built in 1989. And that pic was taken last week.<BR>||||reg||1
