Z||000045||Hock||04-29-2000||04:09 AM||||Its good to see that in my absense that the racing is still as good. Damn good kill cutter. But, I only have one problem. since I've joined the Marine Corps I learned to look before I judge. Don't get me wrong, I'm still as pro Fiero as ever (even though I have for the time retired my efforts). Now I'm in Okinawa, Japan and I have seen alot of cars that would blow alot of your minds away. Must have turbos and the ones that don't still have alot of ass behind them. <P>This brings me to realize that we have alot of work to do. Most of that needs to come from the aftermarket world, btu then the rest needs to come from us. Things that I would suggest: 1)Research new parts that are brought out for other GM vehicles and see what relation that they might have with the Fiero. 2)Read up on the new competition that Japan is building for us. ie: S2000. 3)Always have a back up. What do I mean by that? Try nitrous, turbo, blower, racing fuel, and other things like that.<P>Just a few words of wisdom from the little time I have been here in Japan.<BR> ||||reg||14
Z||000046||Hock||04-29-2000||04:11 AM||||Its good to see that in my absense that the racing is still as good. Damn good kill cutter. But, I only have one problem. since I've joined the Marine Corps I learned to look before I judge. Don't get me wrong, I'm still as pro Fiero as ever (even though I have for the time retired my efforts). Now I'm in Okinawa, Japan and I have seen alot of cars that would blow alot of your minds away. Must have turbos and the ones that don't still have alot of ass behind them. <P>This brings me to realize that we have alot of work to do. Most of that needs to come from the aftermarket world, btu then the rest needs to come from us. Things that I would suggest: 1)Research new parts that are brought out for other GM vehicles and see what relation that they might have with the Fiero. 2)Read up on the new competition that Japan is building for us. ie: S2000. 3)Always have a back up. What do I mean by that? Try nitrous, turbo, blower, racing fuel, and other things like that.<P>Just a few words of wisdom from the little time I have been here in Japan.<BR> ||||reg||14
